  "lesson": {
    "instructions": "First prepare the D-G change, then join the full fingerstyle tune. Melody attacks stay on numbered beats, with gentler eighth-note open-string fills on the and. Keep original half-note endings. Let strings ring naturally where comfortable. Use the written G, C and open-D basses. After the preparation, play the complete twelve-bar tune twice, with one full rest bar between the performances. The first full tune starts at bar 6, including the two count-in bars. Vertically aligned TAB numbers play together. Play only written notes; unclear voices may remain yellow.",
